From 0dc3c4c8e7a55c35fc7f3f9b742a2cc1042b9a70 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Craterbrain <58347640+Craterbrain@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 23:32:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 69/75] PlaitOS: long-press recents action; pocket mode on by
 default

- 3-button navigation: a long press on recents runs the action chosen in
  Settings.System plait_recents_long_press_action (same list as home and
  back). The recents button has no key code, so NavigationBar injects an
  APP_SWITCH down flagged LONG_PRESS plus a canceled up (FLAG_FROM_SYSTEM);
  PhoneWindowManager consumes both in interceptKeyBeforeQueueing, before the
  key gesture handling would open recents, and runs the action on its
  handler. Unset, the listener returns false and the press stays a click;
  during screen pinning the stock back+recents exit is unchanged
- Pocket mode (plait_pocket_judge) defaults to on, as asked; long-press power
  still always leaves the pocket lock

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WNZzm3ssZ7eH5QDg4P9AiP
